1
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:12,920
Turn on the lights and try stepping away.

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,700
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,460
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:47,720
So, on the arcade guide tiles,

6
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black parts.

7
00:00:56,280 --> 00:01:01,760
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

8
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:09,080
Even the self-important politicians
and the blue-eyeshadowed aunties.

9
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning at that corner.

10
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

11
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:27,800
There's a turtle there
(Kame-ari)! Surely there's a turtle!

12
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:32,980
Everyone, come on over to our town.

13
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you.

14
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,500
The island cop returns!

15
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:48,300
The Sydney Olympics start tomorrow, finally!

16
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:51,060
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

17
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:56,700
I have a feeling something important
happened in the last Olympic year...

18
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,240
You said the same thing about Atlanta,
didn't you?

19
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,860
Didn't we talk about cicadas, by the way?

20
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,260
Cicadas?

21
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,980
I'm starting to remember!

22
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:09,660
Aburazemi, minminzemi,

23
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:12,020
tsukutsuku-bōshi, higurashi

24
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,080
Higurashi!

25
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:17,960
sleeping for four years,
waking for just one day,

26
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:20,440
he solves every unsolved case.

27
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,460
The psychic police officer!

28
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,700
You're Higurashi Neruo, right?

29
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,240
Chief.

30
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:39,320
It's been four years, so Ryotsu, could you go wake up Higurashi tomorrow?
Me again? Waking him up is such a pain.

31
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:48,120
Come to think of it, waking him up four years ago was a pain too.
Just thinking about going back into that room again gives me the creeps.

32
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:56,760
Wait, where is Higurashi-san now?
Where? He's at Nikoniko Dormitory, of course. I remember now.

33
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:02,120
When the dormitory was renovated, we accidentally
threw Higurashi-san out with the trash.

34
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:06,140
So he woke up on Yumenoshima,
and that caused a huge mess, didn't it?

35
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:08,020
I see.

36
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:11,080
So what happened after that, Chief?

37
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:15,460
Idiot! Since Higurashi's room
at Nikoniko Dormitory was gone...

38
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:18,060
It was you who handed him over to headquarters,
you idiot.

39
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:21,800
That's right. The Spirit
Investigation Room at headquarters.

40
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:27,200
That's why you're going to headquarters
tomorrow to wake Higurashi up.

41
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,640
Got it, Ryotsu?

42
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,900
Yeah, yeah, I got it.

43
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:35,380
Why do I have to go wake Higurashi up?

44
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:37,800
Still, Higurashi has it made, doesn't he?

45
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,980
He just sleeps all the
time and still gets paid.

46
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:46,680
Wait, now that I think about it, four
years ago, before Higurashi fell asleep,

47
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:51,300
Ryo, I'm worried, so could you hold
on to my important savings passbook?

48
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:55,660
No thief would be scared to come into this room,
I'd think.

49
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:57,320
It's just in case.

50
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,680
Well, good night.

51
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:02,480
This passbook must be that important

52
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:04,440
It's not like there's much in it, right?

53
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:07,760
Thirty million yen?

54
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:11,400
That day was a sure-bet race day.

55
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:15,700
If I put in all 30 million,
it should've doubled to 60 million.

56
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:20,120
If I quietly put back 30 million out of the 60 million,
nobody would notice.

57
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:25,720
Then the horse fell,
and 30 million yen went poof!

58
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:29,180
I felt bad about what I'd done
and agonized over it all night,

59
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:31,960
but the next day I forgot all about it.

60
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:36,800
Uh-oh, if he finds out
I embezzled the money...

61
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:39,760
Hey, how dare you spend my money!

62
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:45,020
I have to do something, or I'm dead meat.

63
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,036
Ryotsu,

64
00:05:03,086 --> 00:05:07,220
if it works, you'll really give me the
money for the overseas couple's trip, right?

65
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:07,604
Hey,

66
00:05:07,654 --> 00:05:12,000
I'll even let you go on a 2001 space odyssey with Jodie,
if you want.

67
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,600
A space trip Not bad.

68
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:16,920
Then I'm counting on you.

69
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:39,760
What was that noise?

70
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:41,600
That was a pretty loud one.

71
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,500
No idea.

72
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:11,800
I'm pretty sure I put it
somewhere around here...

73
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:15,300
Ugh... whoa!

74
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:19,300
Wrong room. It was the one next door.

75
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,180
Is he really still alive like this?

76
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:27,980
Stop gawking and get him out of here quick.

77
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:33,340
What is this room?

78
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:36,740
My senior told me to
recreate Higurashi's room.

79
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,260
And this is the finishing touch.

80
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,840
Did he really live in a room like this?

81
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:45,900
Perfect.

82
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:50,420
Then if we rush-build a police box in the dorm yard,
we're all set.

83
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:52,080
Build a police box?

84
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:56,380
A Nikoniko Dorm-front police box?

85
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:59,520
Alright, that's everything ready.

86
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:03,160
Then I'll go wake Higurashi.

87
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:05,440
You two, stick to the plan.

88
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:06,160
Yes, sir.

89
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,400
Hey, wake up, Higurashi.

90
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:12,960
Ugh, I'm still so sleepy.

91
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:16,340
Come on, get up!
The Sydney Olympics have started!

92
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:18,800
You're old enough to work, you know!

93
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,260
The Sydney Olympics?

94
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:25,260
Wasn't it the Sydney Olympics
the last time he woke up, too?

95
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,952
Gulp! When we woke him
up a year and a half ago,

96
00:07:28,002 --> 00:07:30,180
didn't we cover it up by saying that?

97
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:34,161
Ha your imagination!
Now it's the real, genuine,

98
00:07:34,211 --> 00:07:35,460
year 2000.

99
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:37,500
The Olympics start today, too!

100
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:40,080
Something seems off.

101
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,500
Nothing's off.

102
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:44,220
Come on, hurry up and take a bath.

103
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:47,540
Change into your uniform
and let's get to work, work!

104
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,520
The sun is so bright.

105
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:54,620
See?

106
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,120
You've really gone all out.

107
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:59,820
We've been waking you up every four years.

108
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:01,180
We've gotten used to it.

109
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:02,780
Come on, let's go.

110
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:04,540
Isn't it this way?

111
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:09,460
Why is there a police box
in front of the dormitory?

112
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,584
It moved here while you were sleeping,

113
00:08:12,634 --> 00:08:16,040
changing from Kōen-mae Police Box
to Niconico Dormitory-mae Police Box.

114
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:19,680
Good morning, everyone.

115
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,880
Good morning.

116
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:25,500
Honda, when did you get
transferred to the police box?

117
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:28,680
There was a reassignment
while you were sleeping.

118
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:31,760
And this is Volvo Saigo, the new recruit.

119
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,781
Nice to meet you, Mr. Higurashi.

120
00:08:33,831 --> 00:08:36,120
I've heard all about you
from Squad Leader Ryotsu.

121
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:39,140
Ryotsu's the squad leader?
What about Chief Ohara?

122
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:43,680
He was transferred to the new police box,
so I became squad leader in his place.

123
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:46,400
Looks like he's still dreaming.

124
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,719
Hey, don't you dare fall asleep!

125
00:08:48,769 --> 00:08:51,800
There are some things I need you
to do with your psychic powers.

126
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:53,620
Precognition!

127
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:55,814
I can see it! I can see it!

128
00:08:55,864 --> 00:08:58,820
Japan's national soccer team
is going to the World Cup!

129
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,400
That came out two years ago, though.

130
00:09:03,020 --> 00:09:05,440
Dangorta might become a huge hit.

131
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:08,340
That kind of boom ended long ago.

132
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:13,420
It's been made into a movie,
and even a stage play!

133
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:16,300
Maybe the people's taxes
will be used properly.

134
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:18,900
I don't think that's possible at all.

135
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,980
I just woke up, so I'm not in the mood.

136
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,560
Can't be helped.

137
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,200
Should I go train for your sake?

138
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,460
Training.

139
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,500
Go, Higurashi!

140
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:40,480
That's the spirit, keep going!

141
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,000
With Higurashi's psychic powers,

142
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,960
the 30 million yen he embezzled

143
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,800
is easy to recover, with change to spare.

144
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:52,320
What? Ryotsu's absent?

145
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:54,120
He called this morning,

146
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:57,640
apparently down with a 43-degree fever.

147
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:00,280
They say fools never catch colds.

148
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,840
He's obviously taking a fishing day off.

149
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:12,660
I brought the unsolved case files, thinking he could solve them.
What should we do? Higurashi can only work today.

150
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:19,220
Forget about Ryo-san. Let's go wake Higurashi ourselves. Let's go,
let's go.

151
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:29,380
Being able to list the same person's features, psychic powers really are amazing.
Thanks for your hard work, senior. Well, we have patrol, so we're off.

152
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:31,000
Right, good work.

153
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,860
Hey, don't forget that matter.

154
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,520
Leave it to me.

155
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:41,760
Well then, let's get to the main topic.

156
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:44,140
Where are the unsolved investigation files?

157
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,460
There are no files.

158
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:48,040
I want you to do psychic photography.

159
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:50,140
What am I supposed to
psychically photograph?

160
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:52,420
It's the culprit in the Ogon Ryo case.

161
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:55,060
He's a big gambling fan, you see.

162
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:58,300
I think he's definitely coming
to tomorrow's horse races.

163
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:10,920
Through undercover work, we've learned the culprit is always seen near the finish line board.
So I want you to psychically photograph the moment the horses cross the finish line in races 1 through 12.

164
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:16,320
So the culprit might be in those photos Yeah,
can you do it?

165
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:19,740
I see it!

166
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:22,920
Whoa!

167
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,800
Is race 1 3-8?

168
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:34,540
3-8 is,

169
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:37,660
isn't that a 130-times jackpot ticket?

170
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:45,940
Race 10 is 5-1-3 at 52 times.

171
00:11:46,860 --> 00:11:48,740
Race 11 is 2-4,

172
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:50,180
that's my second jackpot ticket!

173
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:53,600
It's over.

174
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:55,460
I'm finished.

175
00:11:55,460 --> 00:11:57,160
Good work, thanks for your effort.

176
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:01,920
The final race is 7-8, at 5.5 times?

177
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:07,040
The first race at 130 times, multiplied by

178
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:09,820
the second race at 12 times, multiplied by

179
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:12,160
this way, and then that happens

180
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,320
Uh-oh, the display can't show it all

181
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,220
God, oh God

182
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,460
99 trillion 260 billion times

183
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:21,620
if you start by buying a 100-yen
ticket and keep rolling it over

184
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:24,320
that's 9,926 trillion yen, isn't it?

185
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:29,180
Now that I think about it, I feel like I asked
Ryotsu for something before I went to sleep

186
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:31,560
It's the Japan Series, obviously

187
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:33,220
It's the Japan Series

188
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:36,140
No, sorry, the video recorder broke on me

189
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:38,820
it's been broken for four years,
so I couldn't record anything

190
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:41,180
That's too bad

191
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:43,220
No, sorry, sorry

192
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:45,800
Didn't I leave something with Ryotsu

193
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:49,640
Last year was a real mess because of the Y2K problem,
you know

194
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:53,680
Computers all over the world malfunctioned and the world fell into chaos,
or what?

195
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:57,220
No, nothing major happened.

196
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,320
Were missiles launched?

197
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:02,160
Good thing nothing happened.

198
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:04,640
Oh right, the savings.

199
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:07,520
Hey, Higurashi, aren't you thirsty?

200
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:09,100
Yeah, I am.

201
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:11,220
I'll go get you some juice.

202
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,500
Then use this one.

203
00:13:15,260 --> 00:13:17,600
Whoa, you're carrying quite a lot of cash!

204
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:21,380
I fell asleep the day after I got my paycheck,
so I haven't spent any of it.

205
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:23,140
Let me take a look.

206
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:27,860
There's 200,000 here!

207
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:30,120
If we pour this money into horse racing,

208
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,660
it'd become an astronomical sum.

209
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:36,440
Higurashi, these bills are old and no good.

210
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:39,040
Because there were so many
counterfeit bills going around,

211
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:41,460
the bills were switched
to new ones six months ago.

212
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:43,740
I'll exchange them for new bills for you.

213
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:44,600
Here.

214
00:13:45,260 --> 00:13:47,040
They're definitely new bills!

215
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:48,940
And they're 2,000-yen bills!

216
00:13:48,940 --> 00:13:52,680
But I'm sure I gave you 200,000 yen.

217
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,400
You didn't know?

218
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:59,440
When the new bills came out,
Japan also switched to denomination.

219
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:01,460
Denomination?

220
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:03,980
Yeah, basically the unit
dropped by two places.

221
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:06,380
What used to be 100 yen is now 1 yen.

222
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:09,140
One million yen became ten thousand yen.

223
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,520
I didn't know.

224
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:13,360
The world has changed that much?

225
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:16,500
Anyway, I'll buy you some juice,
so wait here.

226
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,120
He's gone!

227
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:21,820
Higurashi's not here!

228
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:23,660
He must have already woken up.

229
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,100
That can't be right.

230
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:29,020
Higurashi-san never wakes up
until a senior officer wakes him.

231
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:31,260
Ryotsu should have woken him.

232
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,520
It's Ryotsu.

233
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:34,380
It must be his doing.

234
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,700
I wonder if some major
incident has happened.

235
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:44,040
If someone broke into headquarters, I don't
think one senior officer could have done it alone.

236
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:46,920
So that means he has
a specialist accomplice.

237
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,840
Anyway, let's go check on Ryo.

238
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:50,660
W-wait a second!

239
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:51,920
They already know.

240
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:56,060
What's wrong, Higurashi?

241
00:14:56,800 --> 00:15:00,500
What's this idol?
Another one that came over from Okinawa?

242
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:03,320
That's Morning Musume.

243
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:06,920
Tsunku from Sharan Q produced them,
and they're a huge hit.

244
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:11,040
I think they started with five members,
and then it grew to eight.

245
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:17,420
After that, one left, another joined, then
three more were added, and five more after that.

246
00:15:17,420 --> 00:15:20,840
I think they're up to
about fifty members now.

247
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,460
R-really?

248
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:25,140
Personally, I think this girl is the best.

249
00:15:25,940 --> 00:15:29,100
That's Mari Goto,
who's making her solo debut soon.

250
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,020
Mari-chan.

251
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:32,760
She's incredibly cute.

252
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:35,320
Well, let's get back to the investigation.

253
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:38,380
Honestly, Higurashi,
you're such a pushover for women.

254
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:41,100
What now?

255
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:43,320
Apparently Mari-chan
is appearing live on TV.

256
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:45,960
Ryotsu, let's go see the TV station!

257
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,180
No, no.

258
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:49,760
You're only awake for today, you know.

259
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:52,060
What I need you to do is...

260
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:53,980
Hello?

261
00:15:53,980 --> 00:15:56,800
Oh no, senpai, we've already been found out!

262
00:15:57,220 --> 00:15:59,720
Chief Ohara and the others
are heading your way right now.

263
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:01,160
Got it.

264
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:02,440
We're getting out of here.

265
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:05,360
Listen,
you just pretend you don't know anything.

266
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:06,040
But...

267
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:06,900
Understood?

268
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:09,180
Higurashi-kun.

269
00:16:09,180 --> 00:16:12,460
Let's go see Mari-chan!

270
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:15,820
If that happens, hurry and call me.

271
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:22,720
Isn't he here?

272
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:23,980
Honda-san's room is...

273
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:26,260
What happened, Nakagawa?

274
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:30,060
He probably used it as a
trick to fool Higurashi-san.

275
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:33,040
It's like something out of Mission:
Impossible.

276
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:37,880
What's wrong?

277
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:41,420
He escaped!

278
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:44,320
Nobody's home

279
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:46,240
This is...

280
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:49,540
Chief, take a look at this.

281
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:56,800
So Ryotsu tricked Higurashi into
predicting tomorrow's horse races.

282
00:16:57,140 --> 00:16:59,480
That's exactly the kind of
thing a senior like him would do.

283
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:01,880
Yes.

284
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,440
Just as I expected, we got in easily.

285
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,880
But it seems he doesn't
know where Ryo-chan is.

286
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:11,460
Now all we can do is catch Honda-san.

287
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:15,500
Ryotsu! Even if I have to tear up every blade of grass,
I'll catch him!

288
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,820
Alright, last challenger Shimizu,
there's no time left, just 10 seconds!

289
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:26,460
Let's do it, let's do it!

290
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:28,240
This is our chance, all or nothing!

291
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:30,420
Yes! We did it!

292
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,740
Congratulations!

293
00:17:32,740 --> 00:17:34,680
You've won the prize money of 1 million yen!

294
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:35,500
Thank you very much!

295
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:41,020
Mr. Shimizu, besides the prize money,
there's still a wonderful present for you!

296
00:17:41,020 --> 00:17:46,100
Today's special guest is
Mari Goto from Morning Musume!

297
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,780
It's the real Mari-chan!

298
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,460
Congratulations!

299
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:59,760
If I succeed,
I'll get that kind of treat from Mari-chan?

300
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:02,360
Then let's move on to the next challenge.

301
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:03,740
The next challenge is...

302
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:05,260
Action!

303
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:08,700
It's a full 50 meters high.

304
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:11,320
If you can dive off
the top of that platform,

305
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,660
the prize is 1 million yen.

306
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:15,900
Now, anyone brave enough to compete,
please come up on stage!

307
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,360
Yes!

308
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:19,060
Ryo-san, aren't you going to take part?

309
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:23,220
A million yen, plus a kiss from Mari-chan!

310
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:26,580
I don't care about the kiss,
but a million yen is nice, isn't it?

311
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:30,820
A million right in front of me beats some billionaire tomorrow,
after all.

312
00:18:30,820 --> 00:18:32,040
Alright, I'm going.

313
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:34,780
Chief, Reiko, and Honda-san

314
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:37,760
We've been asking around,
but they don't know where Senpai went.

315
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:41,440
Damn Ryotsu, where on earth did he go?

316
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:43,520
All the contestants have been assembled.

317
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:44,540
How on earth did he get that money?

318
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:47,420
Knowing Senpai,
he must be up to something outrageous.

319
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:50,000
Or do you want Mari-chan's kiss?

320
00:18:51,860 --> 00:18:54,260
Ryo-chan and Higurashi are on TV!

321
00:18:54,380 --> 00:18:54,960
What?!

322
00:18:56,060 --> 00:18:58,640
I can't believe he's really
doing something so outrageous...

323
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:01,000
Alright, let's rush to the TV station!

324
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,460
I-I'll take the risk!

325
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,720
M-me too...

326
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:13,280
Maybe I'll take the risk too?

327
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:14,860
Me too...

328
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:16,220
No, it's cold...

329
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
You bunch of cowards!

330
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,160
Higurashi, looks like it's
a showdown between you and me.

331
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,660
I'll take Mari-chan's dive.

332
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:24,600
Hah!

333
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:27,740
Higurashi-san jumped!

334
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:30,900
Yeah!

335
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:38,760
Wow! A perfect entry,
barely making a splash!

336
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:42,100
Higurashi, you used psychic powers!

337
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:45,480
Well, whatever.
I could dive from that height too.

338
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:47,100
Alright!

339
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:53,100
Chief

340
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,760
Ryotsu, get down here already!

341
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:57,840
Chief Ohara?

342
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:00,620
Weren't you transferred to
the remote Saihate police box?

343
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:03,700
Igaraji, you've been fooled by Ryotsu.

344
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:06,980
I'm still the squad leader of
the Kameari Park police box.

345
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:11,940
Didn't the Kameari Park police
box move to Nikoniko Ryo-mae?

346
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:13,160
That's a lie too.

347
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:16,140
That police box was a
fake that Ryo-chan made.

348
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,760
What about when they issued the 2000
yen note and it was redenominated?

349
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,840
That's a total lie too!

350
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:25,440
Honda and Volvo confessed everything.

351
00:20:25,980 --> 00:20:27,840
You'd better give up already.

352
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:29,460
Hmm

353
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:31,220
Ugh...

354
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:34,580
Heave-ho!

355
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:36,020
Living the good life, you bastard!

356
00:20:36,140 --> 00:20:38,260
It's the chief and the others who are lying!

357
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:39,740
Trust me!

358
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:43,500
Then what about the 30 million yen
savings passbook I left with you?

359
00:20:44,340 --> 00:20:47,020
That's why I was going to win
it back at the races tomorrow...

360
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,280
So you really did con us!

361
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:50,200
Reiko-san!

362
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:56,040
Dangerous, dangerous!

363
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:58,660
Nooo! Tatagonyan!

364
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:00,560
Too easy!

365
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:06,760
Wow! Roll the camera! Camera!

366
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:09,860
You're not getting away!

367
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,080
Things have taken a turn for the worse!

368
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,960
Higurashi-san turns out to be a psychic!

369
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,740
Starting today,
the Sydney Olympics will be held.

370
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:22,700
And now, the winner, Kimura-kun.

371
00:21:24,620 --> 00:21:26,280
Today's weather highlights are

372
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:35,540
The spherical observation deck has fallen!

373
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:39,020
Right now, something is in front of us...

374
00:21:39,020 --> 00:21:40,420
Ryo's the face of it!

375
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:44,627
Ryo-san,

376
00:21:44,677 --> 00:21:48,280
I'll finish you off with the
most powerful blow there is!

377
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:51,940
Stop it, Higurashi! If you go any further,

378
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:01,020
can't you hear me telling you to stop?

379
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:04,240
It's no use, Chief,
he's not listening anymore.

380
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:08,154
Higurashi is weak when it comes to women,

381
00:22:08,204 --> 00:22:09,860
especially Mari Goto.

382
00:22:11,460 --> 00:22:13,300
Mari-san, pray with us!

383
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:18,160
Higurashi-kun!

384
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:26,740
Higurashi-san, please calm your anger!

385
00:22:26,740 --> 00:22:33,540
Higurashi-kun!

386
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:34,220
Please!

387
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:35,540
Big brother!

388
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:58,500
He's back to normal!

389
00:23:01,060 --> 00:23:03,020
M-Mari-chan.

390
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:05,300
Yes?

391
00:23:05,860 --> 00:23:07,260
Can I have your autograph?

392
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:10,420
Here you go.

393
00:23:12,020 --> 00:23:13,280
Thank you, I'm so happy.

394
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:15,440
Higurashi!

395
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:18,540
Higurashi, don't fall asleep!

396
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:21,180
You haven't done any work yet, you know!

397
00:23:21,180 --> 00:23:23,720
Higurashi, wake up! Higurashi!

398
00:23:24,180 --> 00:23:25,200
Please, wake up!

399
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:29,800
Higurashi's four years' worth of salary

400
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:32,040
will be deducted from my monthly pay.

401
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:33,920
It's only natural.

402
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:36,060
Higurashi fell asleep after that,

403
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:38,840
and he hasn't solved a single case.

404
00:23:38,840 --> 00:23:42,160
And we've also received an
invoice from the TV station.

405
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:42,800
No way.

406
00:23:44,220 --> 00:23:46,860
Well, that's how it is,
so hurry up and get out of the hospital

407
00:23:46,860 --> 00:23:48,740
and get to work properly.

408
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:51,560
What a disaster.

409
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:54,020
This is just adding insult to injury.

410
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:55,940
Well then, everyone,

411
00:23:55,940 --> 00:23:58,220
see you in 2004.

412
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:28,200
Thank you for watching.

413
00:24:28,220 --> 00:24:30,560
Though people seem composed on the surface,

414
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:33,300
with a beef bowl and extra broth,

415
00:24:33,980 --> 00:24:36,640
the irritation from endless overtime

416
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:40,260
melts away with ylang-ylang.

417
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:46,320
Every day, no problem.

418
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:50,040
Once you pass through a hot shower,

419
00:24:50,040 --> 00:24:53,080
every day, no problem.

420
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:56,660
an anmin pillow restores your energy.

421
00:24:59,860 --> 00:25:02,640
Every day, no problem-brain.

422
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:06,240
I love this version of me.

423
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:09,460
Every day, no problem-brain.

424
00:25:09,460 --> 00:25:13,080
Monday with hearts flying around.

425
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:17,460
Monday, Monday, no problem-brain.

426
00:25:19,800 --> 00:25:21,880
Where on earth are we?

427
00:25:23,080 --> 00:25:26,100
Did we time-slip half
a century into the past?

428
00:25:26,420 --> 00:25:27,000
What?

429
00:25:27,220 --> 00:25:28,300
Doinaken?

430
00:25:28,540 --> 00:25:30,200
I've never heard of a place like that!

431
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:33,640
Whatever, but why would
something like that even come up!

432
00:25:34,140 --> 00:25:36,600
Next time, the remote region of Doinaken.

433
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:37,580
See you then!

434
00:25:38,600 --> 00:25:40,800
Over there is Kameari.

435
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:44,180
Well, it's definitely Kameari.

436
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:49,160
Everyone, come on over to our town!

437
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:50,740
Thank you!

438
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:54,000
Thank you for watching.

